{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01WcSXniAkhGp1y1Yqfv8RuF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 2: Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source (coreutils, moreutils, grep, findutils), generates Go implementations via an AI orchestrator, and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**:\n- `cmd/` — one package per utility, each with `main.go` and `_test.go`\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness (RunDiffTests, TimestampNormalizer)\n- `pkg/sys/` — portable syscall abstractions (terminal width, extended stat, signals)\n- `pkg/format/` — shared formatting (columns, ANSI color, human-readable sizes)\n- `magefiles/` — mage build targets; cobbler:measure/stitch drive the generation cycle\n- `docs/` — PRDs, use cases, test suites (all specs)\n\n**Current state**: Working branch has specs only. Generated code (pkg/testutils, cmd/ts, cmd/cat, cmd/wc, cmd/sponge, pkg/sys, pkg/format) lives at generation-merged tags, not on the working branch.\n\n**Current release**: rel01.0 (in_progress) — ts specification and differential test. Use case rel01.0-uc001-ts is in_progress.\n\n**Existing open issues**:\n1. `generation-2026-02-26-21-54-45-25b` — Implement pkg/testutils (prd001 R1-R5)\n2. `generation-2026-02-26-21-54-45-g8q` — Implement cmd/ts (prd004-ts R1-R8)\n\n## Step 3: Priority Reasoning\n\nrel01.0 requires: pkg/testutils + cmd/ts implementation + cmd/ts differential tests. Issues 25b and g8q cover the implementation tasks. **prd004-ts R9 (differential tests for cmd/ts) is not covered by any existing issue.** That is the gap — the test file `cmd/ts/ts_test.go` that calls RunDiffTests with the 13 cases from test-rel01.0.\n\nThis task depends on 25b (pkg/testutils) and g8q (cmd/ts main.go) being resolved first, expressed via required_reading.\n\n## Step 4 & 5: Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/ts differential tests (prd004-ts R9)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd004-ts.yaml (R9 differential testing requirements)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.0.yaml (all 13 test cases with inputs and expected outputs)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (DiffTest struct contract R1, RunDiffTests R2-R3, TimestampNormalizer R4)\n      - cmd/ts/main.go (binary entry point being tested -- must exist before this task runs)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (RunDiffTests and TimestampNormalizer API -- must exist before this task runs)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ts/ts_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests for cmd/ts against the reference ts binary using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement TestMain in cmd/ts/ts_test.go that builds the cmd/ts binary into a temp directory via exec.Command(\\\"go\\\", \\\"build\\\", \\\"-o\\\", goBinaryPath, \\\".\\\") before any test runs. Store the resulting binary path in a package-level variable. Locate the reference binary ts using exec.LookPath(\\\"ts\\\"); call m.Run() and skip all tests with t.Skip if ts is not found.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement TestTs(t *testing.T) that defines a []testutils.DiffTest slice covering all 13 test cases from test-rel01.0 and calls testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinaryPath, refBinaryPath, tests). Each DiffTest entry must have a Name field matching the test-rel01.0 test case name exactly: default_format_three_lines, default_format_empty_stdin, default_format_partial_last_line, custom_strftime_format, subsecond_format_dotS, elapsed_since_start_mode, incremental_mode, incremental_and_elapsed_mutually_exclusive, monotonic_clock_mode, relative_mode_syslog_timestamp, relative_mode_no_timestamp_passthrough, invalid_flag, tz_environment_respected (prd004-ts R9.2).\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Apply pkg/testutils.TimestampNormalizer (a slice of Normalize functions per prd001-testutils R4.3) to all DiffTest cases whose stdout contains wall-clock timestamps: default_format_three_lines, default_format_partial_last_line, custom_strftime_format, subsecond_format_dotS, elapsed_since_start_mode, incremental_mode, monotonic_clock_mode, relative_mode_syslog_timestamp, and tz_environment_respected. Set Normalize to nil for default_format_empty_stdin, relative_mode_no_timestamp_passthrough, incremental_and_elapsed_mutually_exclusive, and invalid_flag (prd004-ts R9.1).\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Set the Env field on each DiffTest to include LC_ALL=C. For tz_environment_respected, also include TZ=UTC. For elapsed_since_start_mode and incremental_mode, also include TZ=GMT to match the Perl reference behavior (prd004-ts R3.2, R4.2, R8.1).\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"For incremental_and_elapsed_mutually_exclusive and invalid_flag, set ExpectedExitCode to a non-zero value. These cases must verify that the process exits non-zero; do not apply normalization. For all other cases, set ExpectedExitCode to 0 (prd004-ts R3.4, R7.2).\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Set Stdin to the correct []byte for each test case as specified in test-rel01.0. For default_format_empty_stdin, set Stdin to []byte{} (empty but non-nil, per prd001-testutils R1.2). For test cases with no stdin (nil in test-rel01.0), set Stdin to nil.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"TimestampNormalizer from pkg/testutils replaces strftime-formatted timestamp prefixes with a fixed placeholder. Pass it as a slice ([]testutils.Normalize{testutils.TimestampNormalizer}) in the Normalize field of each DiffTest that requires normalization, per prd001-testutils R4.3.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Build the binary in TestMain using os.MkdirTemp for a throwaway directory and defer os.RemoveAll to clean up after all tests complete. Set the package-level variable before calling m.Run().\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"The Args field in each DiffTest must contain only the flags and positional arguments passed to the binary -- do not include the binary name itself. The binary paths are passed separately to RunDiffTests per prd001-testutils R2.1.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/ts/... passes with no failures when both the Go ts binary builds successfully and the reference ts binary (from moreutils) is on PATH.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"All 13 test cases from test-rel01.0 are present as named DiffTest entries. The Name field of each entry matches the test_case name from test-rel01.0 exactly.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"When the reference ts binary is not found on PATH, all tests are skipped via t.Skip with a message indicating ts is not installed, rather than failing.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"TimestampNormalizer is applied to every test case that produces wall-clock timestamp output. Test cases with deterministic or error output have nil normalization.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"cmd/ts/ts_test.go compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72940,"cache_read_input_tokens":15559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72940},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab9589cf-d97d-440c-97ad-a466161e2a02","uuid":"76edee75-d841-4664-be09-31303e204b94"}
